{"availability":"available","full":"TimJJTing/Escaping-Flatland","name":"Escaping-Flatland","description":"A demo of optimization techniques for plotting large datasets in a 3D space using Three.js + Svelte integration","category":"Developer tools","language":"Svelte","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-10-23T16:51:29Z","updated":"2026-05-16T17:13:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://escaping-flatland.netlify.app","topics":["big-data","data-visualization","glsl-shaders","lod","octree","svelte","sveltekit","three-js"],"demo":"https://escaping-flatland.netlify.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.464Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.464Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.464Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.464Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js","Svelte"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["“Even though we navigate daily through a perceptual world of three dimensions… the world displayed on our information displays is caught up in the two dimensionality of the endless flatlands of paper and video screens… Escaping this flatland is the essential task of envisioning information — for all the interesting worlds that we seek to understand are inevitably and happily multivariate in nature. Not flatlands.” (Tufte 1990)","Computer screens have the ability to display a wide range of information. Beyond 3D coordinates, they can simultaneously show colors, dynamic patterns, rotations, and motions, enabling human eyes to observe and interpret complex datasets.","This project renders particles in real time inside a browser using Three.js and a sparse Octree. You can orbit the camera, click any star to focus on it and inspect its data (rotation speed, planet count, differential rotation constants), and watch a miniature solar system appear around your selection. It also explores how Three.js can be integrated into a Svelte 5 project, though Threlte offers a more mature solution for this purpose."],"features":["1M particles rendered in real time using instanced meshes and a sparse Octree","Frustum culling — only particles inside the camera view are processed each frame","Three-tier LOD — HD / SD / LD geometry tiers based on distance from camera","Solar system — selected star spawns orbiting planets","Bloom post-processing — selective glow effect with configurable strength"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimJJTing/Escaping-Flatland/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f5a8a3233013c6236c324de520be3f900b115d2d96305f7461180e857f5c8217","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.546Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.546Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"“Even though we navigate daily through a perceptual world of three dimensions… the world displayed on our information displays is caught up in the two dimensionality of the endless flatlands of paper and video screens… Escaping this flatland is the essential task of envisioning information — for all the interesting worlds that we seek to understand are inevitably and happily multivariate in nature. Not flatlands.” (Tufte 1990)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimJJTing/Escaping-Flatland/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f5a8a3233013c6236c324de520be3f900b115d2d96305f7461180e857f5c8217","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimJJTing/Escaping-Flatland/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.546Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-05-16T17:13:28Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TimJJTing/Escaping-Flatland/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T05:43:00.547Z","hash":"f5a8a3233013c6236c324de520be3f900b115d2d96305f7461180e857f5c8217","originalBytes":7627,"storedBytes":7627,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["data","star","camera","run","escaping","docker","build","bash","demo","flatland","index","labels","loading","may","npm","project","rotation","svelte","three.js","dataset","deb